onversations, texts or presentations about common technology."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le06ob10re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to close up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to close a business for the day; to stop operation"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are still a few customers, but I'm going to close up the restaurant at 11 p.m. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le06ob10aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when you talk on the phone."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "What's going on?"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a casual way to ask what's happening or \u201cHow are you?\u201d"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Hi, Sally. Nice to hear from you. What's going on?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le06ob10aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to pass out"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to faint or lose consciousness"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm so tired. I'll pass out if I stay up any longer."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le06ob10aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to go away"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to go out of the city on vacation"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If I went away tomorrow, I would lie on the beach for a week."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le06ob10aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to put up with"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to endure or accept a certain mental or physical condition"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Your body can only put up with so much stress."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le06ob10aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to break down "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to stop functioning normally"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Sooner or later, your body is going to break down from all the stress."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le06ob10aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to turn in "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to go to bed"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm tired, so I'm going to turn in for the night."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le06ob10aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Phrasal Verbs"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " There are various phrasal verbs that are used to talk about different things. Here is list of phrasal verbs for talking on the phone and one list for talking about health."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Phrasal verbs are constructed with:<br/>verb + particle/preposition<br/>The verb by itself has one meaning and takes on a different meaning when put together with the preposition.<br/><br/>Here is list of phrasal verbs for talking on the phone and one list for talking about health."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Phrasal Verb for Talking on the Phone\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to put through\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Could you put me through to the manager?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to hold on\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Please hold on for a moment. I'll see if the manager is available.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to hold on\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Can you speak up? I can't hear you very well.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Phrasal Verb for Talking about Health\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to pass out\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I'm so tired that I will pass out if I stay up any longer.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to knock out\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Since I'm so tired, alcohol would knock me out completely\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to go away\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You'll rest your mind if you go away on vacation for a week.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to put up with\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Your body can only put up with a limited amount of stress.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to break down\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" If you don't get some rest, your body is going to break down.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to turn in\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Maybe you should turn in early and get a good sleep.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Conditional Sentences with If Clauses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "With conditional sentences using <span class=\"italic\">if</span> clauses, one part is the condition and the other part is the result.<br/>Two types of conditional sentences talk about imaginary situations in the future: the first and the second conditional."}, {"type": "text", "content": " Each conditional form uses a different verb form."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Type of Conditional\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Explanation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" First Conditional\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You're talking about the future. There is a real possibility that this condition will happen.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" If + condition in Present Simple, will + base verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\"> <ul><li>If you want to go out, I could meet you.</li> <li>I'll pass out if I stay up any longer.</li> <li>If I drink alcohol, it will knock me out completely.</li></ul></span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Second Conditional\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You're still talking about the future. However, there is <span class=\\\"italic\\\">not</span> a real possibility the condition will happen.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" If + condition in Past Simple, would + base verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><ul><li>If we had a bed on rollers, we could roll you home from the pub.</li> <li>If I went away tomorrow, I would lie on the beach for a week.</li></ul></span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write